@q 49:3-5

**COVID-19** (first reported in Wuhan, December 2019; WHO declared a pandemic on 11 March 2020) is caused by the coronavirus **SARS-CoV-2**. **mRNA vaccines**: Pfizer-BioNTech and **Moderna** (India's Gennova made one too). **Whole inactivated virus**: **Sinovac** (CoronaVac), Sinopharm and **Covaxin** (Bharat Biotech). **Viral vector**: **Covishield** (Oxford-AstraZeneca, made by Serum Institute), Sputnik V. **Protein subunit**: Novavax (Covovax), **Corbevax**. India's **ZyCoV-D** was the world's first DNA vaccine for humans.

@section 26.2 | Mosquito-borne Viral Diseases

@q 49:6-8

@table
Mosquito | Diseases spread
**Aedes aegypti / albopictus** (tiger mosquito; bites by day) | **Dengue, chikungunya, Zika, yellow fever**
**Anopheles** (female) | **Malaria** (protozoan)
**Culex** | **Filaria** (worm), **Japanese encephalitis** (virus)
@end

**Dengue** lowers the **platelet** count (dengue haemorrhagic fever). **Japanese encephalitis** (JE) inflames the brain; pigs act as amplifying hosts and Culex mosquitoes from paddy fields spread it.

@up UP link: **Gorakhpur** and the eastern UP districts long suffered **Japanese encephalitis and acute encephalitis syndrome** outbreaks among children. JE vaccination, cleaner water and the **Dastak** campaign (from 2017) brought cases and deaths down sharply.

@section 26.3 | Other Viral Diseases

@q 49:9-10

**Rabies** (hydrophobia: fear of water) comes from the **bite of infected dogs**, cats or bats; the first vaccine was **Louis Pasteur**'s (1885). India aims to end dog-mediated rabies deaths by 2030. **Meningitis** is swelling of the membranes (meninges) around the brain and spinal cord.

@q 49:11-13

@src1 49:3
@src1 49:4

@one
Jonas Salk is known for the discovery of
@ans Polio vaccine
@end

@one
The Salk vaccine is related to which of the following diseases?
@ans Polio
@end

**Rotavirus** is the leading cause of severe **diarrhoea** in infants; India's own **Rotavac** vaccine is in the immunisation programme. **Polio** spreads through **contaminated food and water**; **Jonas Salk** made the injectable vaccine (1952-55) and **Albert Sabin** the oral drops. **India was declared polio-free in March 2014.**

@q 49:14-16

@q 49:17-21

@table
Virus fact | Detail
**Hepatitis B** | **DNA virus**; affects the **liver**; spread through blood, sex, mother to child; vaccine in UIP
Hepatitis A and E | Spread by contaminated **water and food**
**HIV** (causes **AIDS**) | **RNA retrovirus** (RNA + protein coat; makes DNA with reverse transcriptase); attacks **T4 (CD4) helper cells**
HIV subtype in India | **HIV-1 C**
Discoverers | **Luc Montagnier** (France, 1983) and **Robert Gallo** (USA, HTLV-III, 1984)
Tests | **ELISA** (screening), Western blot (confirmation)
Common cold | **Rhinovirus**
@end

