@qnote 50:3 | The source gives **(a) & (d)**: the bacterium *Haemophilus influenzae* type b (Hib) causes **meningitis** and **pneumonia** in young children; influenza itself is caused by a virus. The **pentavalent** vaccine protects against Hib.

@q 50:9-15

@table
Bacterial disease | Bacterium | Note
**Tuberculosis** | *Mycobacterium tuberculosis* (Robert Koch, 1882) | Affects **lungs**; **BCG** vaccine at birth; **Mantoux** skin test; India targets elimination (TB Mukt Bharat)
**Cholera** | *Vibrio cholerae* | **Waterborne**; ORS saves lives
**Typhoid** | *Salmonella typhi* | Affects the **intestine**; **Widal test**
**Tetanus** | *Clostridium tetani* | **"Lockjaw"**; spores enter wounds
**Diphtheria** | *Corynebacterium diphtheriae* | Throat; **toxoid** vaccine
Whooping cough | *Bordetella pertussis* | Children
**Plague** | *Yersinia pestis* | Spread by **rat fleas**, not mosquitoes
**Leprosy** | *Mycobacterium leprae* | Skin and nerves; India declared it eliminated as a public health problem in 2005
**Botulism** | *Clostridium botulinum* | Deadly **food poisoning** toxin (also "Botox")
Pneumonia | *Streptococcus pneumoniae* and others | **Lungs**
Syphilis | *Treponema pallidum* | Sexual contact
@end

