@ans Polio
@end

@src 50:5
@pyq U.P. P.C.S. (Pre) 2023
Which type of vaccine protects against Diphtheria?
(a) Live-attenuated
(b) Viral Vector
(c) Toxoid
(d) mRNA
@ans (c)
@end

@q 50:6-8

@table
Vaccine / drug | Against / note
**DPT** | **Diphtheria, pertussis (whooping cough), tetanus**; diphtheria and tetanus parts are **toxoids** (inactivated toxins)
**BCG** | **Tuberculosis**, given at birth
OPV / IPV | Polio
MR | Measles and rubella
Pentavalent | DPT + hepatitis B + Hib
**Antibiotics** | Mostly from **bacteria** (*Streptomyces*: streptomycin, tetracycline) and some from **fungi** (penicillin from *Penicillium*)
**Sulpha drugs** | Synthetic **antibacterials** (sulfonamides, e.g. **Cibazol** / sulfathiazole)
Aspirin | Painkiller and fever reducer
@end

The source keys antibiotics as "mostly from bacteria", which is right: about two-thirds come from actinomycete bacteria (*Streptomyces*).

@section 26.6 | Protozoan, Worm and Fungal Diseases

@q 51:1-2

@src 51:3
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2008
Which of the following parasites is responsible for 65% of the cases of malaria in India ?
(a) P. malariae
(b) P. vivax
(c) P. falciparum
(d) P. ovale
@ans (b)
@end

@src 51:4
@pyq U.P.P.C.S. (Pre) 2024
What is R21/Matrix-M^{TM}?
(a) Vaccine against Malaria developed by Serum Institute of India
(b) Vaccine against Malaria developed by Bharat Biotech International
(c) Vaccine against AIDS developed by Serum Institute of India
(d) Vaccine against AIDS developed by Bharat Biotech International
@ans (a)
@end

**Malaria** is caused by the protozoan ***Plasmodium*** and spread by **female Anopheles** mosquitoes. **Ronald Ross** proved the mosquito link in **Secunderabad (1897)** and won the Nobel Prize (1902). In India *P. vivax* causes most cases and *P. falciparum* the dangerous **malignant** (cerebral) malaria. WHO approved **RTS,S** (2021) and **R21/Matrix-M** (2023; Oxford, made by the **Serum Institute of India**) as malaria vaccines. Dengue and malaria share fever and mosquito bites but are spread by **different mosquito species**.

