@q 51:8-10

@table
Cause | Diseases
**Protozoa** | **Malaria** (*Plasmodium*), amoebic dysentery (*Entamoeba*), **sleeping sickness** (*Trypanosoma*, tsetse fly), kala-azar (*Leishmania*, sand fly)
**Worms (helminths)** | **Filaria / elephantiasis** (*Wuchereria*, a nematode spread by Culex), roundworm, hookworm, tapeworm
**Fungi** | Ringworm, **athlete's foot**, dandruff, some **baldness** (tinea capitis), candidiasis
**Bacteria** | **Peptic ulcers** (*Helicobacter pylori*; Nobel 2005)
@end

Fluorosis comes from excess **fluoride** in water, not a germ. Leander Paes's 2003 illness was a brain **cyst** caused by neurocysticercosis, an infection from the **pork tapeworm**.

@trap
**Pandemic = worldwide.** **Aedes = dengue, chikungunya, Zika, yellow fever**; **Culex = JE, filaria**; **Anopheles = malaria**. Dengue lowers **platelets**. **Hepatitis B is a DNA virus**, **HIV an RNA retrovirus**. India's HIV subtype = **1C**. **Rinderpest** was eradicated in 2011. **TB, cholera, typhoid, tetanus, plague, leprosy = bacteria.** **DPT** excludes polio; diphtheria vaccine is a **toxoid**. **R21 = Serum Institute malaria vaccine.** **Peptic ulcer = bacteria.**
@end

@heatmap

@pattern
Disease questions are among the most frequent in the paper, and recent years have shifted to **current health news**: COVID-19 virus and vaccines (2022-2024), malaria vaccine R21 (2024), Nipah (2018), toxoid vaccines and peptic ulcers (2023). The older core (cause of a disease, DPT, BCG, polio, AIDS) still repeats.
@end

@next
Likely next angles: **TB Mukt Bharat** and the 100-day campaign, **Nipah** and **Zika** outbreaks, **H5N1 in mammals**, **mpox** (WHO emergency 2024), **antimicrobial resistance** (Kerala's AMR action, the Red Line campaign), **HPV vaccine** for cervical cancer, **malaria elimination by 2030**, and **U-WIN** vaccination records.
@end
